QuestGuidance.Register("en",239,{
[7617]="700626A0\n1\tYou should speak with the Novice Jeweller to learn more about jewelcrafting.\t\n2\tThe Novice Jeweller provided you with a crate full of ingredients that you can use to execute the copper ring recipe. Open the crate to get the ingredients. Ingredients for Jewellers are normally purchased from vendors or traded from players with the prospector profession. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.\t\n3\tUsing the ingredient you received, craft a copper ring at a workbench\tThe Novice Jeweller provided you with the ingredients necessary to create a copper ring. Approach the workbench and prepare the copper ring. To open your crafting panel, you can use the 'T' key or click on the crafting button (it looks like a hammer and anvil) in the lower left part of your UI. Select the Jeweller tab in the craft UI and find the proper recipe. Remember: in order to execute a recipe, you must be near the proper facility. Jewelcrafting requires a workbench.\n4\tThe recipe is complete. Do not sell the copper ring! It is time to show your handiwork to your mentor, the Novice Jeweller.\t\n",
[7618]="70025AF4\n1\tYou should speak with the Novice Metalsmith to learn more about metalsmithy.\t\n2\tThe Novice Metalsmith provided you with a crate full of ingredients that you can use to execute the bronze helm recipe. Open the crate to get the ingredients. Ingredients for Metalsmiths are normally purchased from vendors or traded from players with the prospector profession. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.\t\n3\tUsing the ingredients you have, forge a bronze helm\tCreate the bronze helm, as instructed by the Novice Metalsmith.\n4\tThe recipe is complete. Do not sell the bronze helm! It is time to show your handiwork to your mentor, the Novice Metalsmith.\t\n",
[7619]="70062697\n1\tYou should speak with the Novice Metalsmith to learn more about metalsmithy.\t\n2\tThe Novice Metalsmith provided you with a crate full of ingredients that you can use to execute the bronze helm recipe. Open the crate to get the ingredients. Ingredients for Metalsmiths are normally purchased from vendors or traded from players with the prospector profession. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.\t\n3\tUsing the ingredients you have, forge a bronze helm at a forge\tCreate the bronze helm, as instructed by the Novice Metalsmith. To open your crafting panel, you can use the 'T' key or click on the crafting button (it looks like a hammer and anvil) in the lower left part of your UI. Select the Metalsmithy tab in the craft UI and find the proper recipe. Remember: In order to execute a recipe, you must be near the proper facility. Metalsmithy requires a forge.\n4\tThe recipe is complete. Do not sell the bronze helm! It is time to show your handiwork to your mentor, the Novice Metalsmith.\t\n",
[7620]="70025AF5\n1\tYou should speak with the supplier to learn more about prospecting.\t\n2\tIngredients for prospectors are found in ore-nodes in the wild, sometimes in chests, and purchased from suppliers. You can also find ingredients in the Auction Hall. The supplier provided you with a crate full of ingredients that you can use to execute the prospector recipe. Open the crate to get the ingredients.\t\n3\tUsing the ingredients you received, craft a copper ingot\tThe Supplier provided you with the ingredients necessary to create a copper ingot.\n4\tThe recipe is complete. Do not sell the copper ingot! It is time to show your handiwork to your mentor, the supplier.\t\n",
[7621]="700626AF\n1\tYou should speak with the chief supplier to learn more about prospecting.\t\n2\tIngredients for prospectors are found in ore-nodes in the wild, sometimes in chests, and purchased from suppliers. You can also find ingredients in the Auction Hall. The supplier provided you with a crate full of ingredients that you can use to execute the prospector recipe. Open the crate to get the ingredients.\t\n3\tUsing the ingredients you received, craft a copper ingot at a forge\tThe Chief Supplier provided you with the ingredients necessary to create a copper ingot. To open your crafting panel, you can use the 'T' key or click on the crafting button (it looks like a hammer and anvil) in the lower left part of your UI. Select the Prospecting tab in the craft UI and find the proper recipe. Remember: in order to execute a recipe you must be near the proper facility. Prospecting requires a forge.\n4\tThe recipe is complete. Do not sell the copper ingot! It is time to show your handiwork to your mentor, the chief supplier.\t\n",
[7622]="70025AF6\n1\tYou should speak with the novice scholar to learn more about scholarship.\t\n2\tThe novice scholar provided you with a crate full of ingredients that you can use to execute the scroll of minor scholar lore recipe. Open the crate to get the ingredients. Ingredients for Scholars are normally purchased from vendors found near ruins, inside chests, or sometimes upon sentient enemies. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.\t\n3\tUsing the ingredients you received, craft a scroll of minor scholar lore\tThe novice scholar provided you with the ingredients necessary to create a scroll of minor scholar lore.\n4\tThe recipe is complete. Do not sell the scroll of minor scholar lore! It is time to show your handiwork to your mentor, the novice scholar.\t\n",
[7623]="70062643\n1\tYou should speak with Meleri to learn more about scholarship.\t\n2\tThe novice scholar provided you with a crate full of ingredients that you can use to execute the scroll of minor scholar lore recipe. Open the crate to get the ingredients. Ingredients for Scholars are normally purchased from vendors found near ruins, inside chests, or sometimes upon sentient enemies. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.\t\n3\tUsing the ingredients you received, craft a scroll of minor scholar lore through the crafting panel\tMeleri, the novice scholar, provided you with the ingredients necessary to create a scroll of minor scholar lore. To open your crafting panel, you can use the 'T' key or click on the crafting button (it looks like a hammer and anvil) in the lower left part of your UI. Select the Scholarship tab in the craft UI and find the proper recipe. Scholarship requires no facilities in early tiers, but will require a study for more advanced recipes.\n4\tThe recipe is complete. Do not sell the scroll of minor scholar lore! It is time to show your handiwork to your mentor, Meleri.\t\n",
[7624]="70025AF7\n1\tYou should speak with the Novice Tailor to learn more about tailoring.\t\n2\tThe Novice Tailor provided you with a crate full of ingredients that you can use to execute the rough cloth cloak recipe. Open the crate to get the ingredients. Ingredients for Tailors are normally purchased from vendors or traded from players with the forester profession. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.\t\n3\tUsing the ingredients you have, craft a rough cloth cloak\tCreate the rough cloth cloak, as instructed by the Novice Tailor.\n4\tThe recipe is complete. Do not sell the rough cloth cloak! It is time to show your handiwork to your mentor, the Novice Tailor.\t\n",
[7625]="70062696\n1\tYou should speak with the Novice Tailor to learn more about tailoring.\t\n2\tThe Novice Tailor provided you with a crate full of ingredients that you can use to execute the rough cloth cloak recipe. Open the crate to get the ingredients. Ingredients for Tailors are normally purchased from vendors or traded from players with the forester profession. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.\t\n3\tUsing the ingredients you have, craft a rough cloth cloak at a workbench\tCreate the rough cloth cloak, as instructed by the Novice Tailor. To open your crafting panel, you can use the 'T' key or click on the crafting button (it looks like a hammer and anvil) in the lower left part of your UI. Select the Tailoring tab in the craft UI and find the proper recipe. Remember: in order to execute a recipe you must be near the proper facility. Tailoring requires a workbench.\n4\tThe recipe is complete. Do not sell the rough cloth cloak! It is time to show your handiwork to your mentor, the Novice Tailor.\t\n",
[7626]="70025AF8\n1\tYou should speak with the Novice Weaponcrafter to learn more about weaponsmithy.\t\n2\tThe Novice Weaponcrafter provided you with a crate full of ingredients that you can use to create a bronze weapon. Open the crate to get the ingredients. Ingredients for Weaponsmiths are normally purchased from vendors or traded from players with the prospecting profession and, in some rare cases, the woodworking profession. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.\t\n3\tCreate a bronze sword, dagger, axe, great sword, or throwing axe, as instructed by the Novice Weaponcrafter.\t\n4\tThe recipe is complete. Do not sell the bronze weapon! It is time to show your handiwork to the Novice Weaponcrafter.\t\n",
[7627]="70062646\n1\tYou should speak with the Novice Weaponcrafter to learn more about weaponsmithy.\t\n2\tThe Novice Weaponcrafter provided you with a crate full of ingredients that you can use to create a bronze weapon. Open the crate to get the ingredients. Ingredients for Weaponsmiths are normally purchased from vendors or traded from players with the prospecting profession and, in some rare cases, the woodworking profession. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.\t\n3\tCreate a bronze sword, dagger, axe, great sword, or throwing axe, as instructed by the Novice Weaponcrafter. To open your crafting panel, you can use the 'T' key or click on the crafting button (it looks like a hammer and anvil) in the lower left part of your UI. Select the Weaponsmithy tab in the craft UI and find the proper recipe. Remember: In order to execute a recipe, you must be near the proper facility. Weaponsmithy requires a forge.\t\n4\tThe recipe is complete. Do not sell the bronze weapon! It is time to show your handiwork to the Novice Weaponcrafter.\t\n",
[7628]="70025AF9\n1\tYou should speak with a Novice Woodworker to learn more about woodworking.\t\n2\tThe Novice Woodworker has provided you with a crate full of ingredients that you can use to execute a rowan weapon recipe. Open the crate to get the ingredients. Ingredients for Woodworkers are normally purchased from vendors or traded from players with the forester profession. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.\t\n3\tCreate a rowan bow, staff, spear, hammer, club, great club, or javelin, as instructed by the Novice Woodworker.\t\n4\tThe recipe is complete. Do not sell the rowan weapon! Time to show your handiwork to your mentor.\t\n",
[7629]="70062695\n1\tYou should speak with a Novice Woodworker to learn more about woodworking.\t\n2\tThe Novice Woodworker has provided you with a crate full of ingredients that you can use to execute a rowan weapon recipe. Open the crate to get the ingredients. Ingredients for Woodworkers are normally purchased from vendors or traded from players with the forester profession. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.\t\n3\tCreate a rowan bow, staff, spear, hammer, club, great club, or javelin, as instructed by the Novice Woodworker. To open your crafting panel, you can use the 'T' key or click on the crafting button (it looks like a hammer and anvil) in the lower left part of your UI. Select the Woodworking tab in the craft UI and find the proper recipe. Remember: In order to execute a recipe, you must be near the proper facility. Woodworking requires a workbench.\t\n4\tThe recipe is complete. Do not sell the rowan weapon! Time to show your handiwork to your mentor.\t\n",
[7630]="700466B1\n1\tImrahil can be found just outside the main gate of after-battle Minas Tirith. You can travel there from the Threshold of the City on the Pelennor battlefield and from pre-battle Minas Tirith. You have been summoned by Imrahil for an important task. The travel horses at pre-battle Minas Tirith are only available if you've completed Volume 4: Book 6, Chapter 8: On a Field of Red of the Epic. Alternatively you may get to the after-battle Minas Tirith from a Minas Tirith stable master.\t\n2\tTalk to Imrahil just outside of after-battle Minas Tirith\tImrahil can be found just outside the main gate of after-battle Minas Tirith. You can travel there from the Threshold of the City on the Pelennor battlefield and from pre-battle Minas Tirith. You have been summoned by Imrahil for an important task. The travel horses at pre-battle Minas Tirith are only available if you've completed Volume 4: Book 6, Chapter 8: On a Field of Red of the Epic. Alternatively you may get to the after-battle Minas Tirith from a Minas Tirith stable master.\n3\tTalk to Aragorn\tAragorn can be found in his pavilion on after-battle Pelennor. You should learn what plans Aragorn has and what help he might need.\n4\tTalk to Éomer\030Talk to Angbor\tAngbor and Éomer can be found at Aragorn's Pavilion on after-battle Pelennor. You should ask Angbor and Éomer whether their men are ready to march.\n",
[7631]="7004123B\n1\tSpeak with Lothíriel about Central Gondor\tLothíriel can be found in the Great Hall of the Prince in Dol Amroth. You have been summoned to Dol Amroth by Lothíriel, who seeks your aid once more.\n2\tTalk to Lothíriel about Central Gondor\tLothíriel can be found in the Great Hall of the Prince in Dol Amroth. You have been summoned to Dol Amroth by Lothíriel, who seeks your aid once more.\n3\tTalk to someone in Ethring in Ringló Vale about aiding Central Gondor\tEthring can be found in the Ringló Vale to the south-east of Lamedon. Lothíriel has asked you to travel into Central Gondor and aid the people of Ringló Vale, Dor-en-Ernil, and Lebennin.\n",
[7632]="700156A7\n1\tTalk to Aesseledh, the Cook's Guild-leader\tAesseledh, the Cook's Guild-leader, is in the Cook's Guild-hall in Michel Delving. The Master of Crafting Guilds has instructed you to speak with Aesseledh to learn more about the Cook's Guild.\n2\tTalk to the repast recipe vendor\tHonesty Goodbody is in the Cook's Guild-hall in Michel Delving. Aesseledh has directed you to speak with Honesty Goodbody to look at what recipes she sells.\n3\tTalk to the vendor who sells improved recipes\tAnnie Hayhurst is in the Cook's Guild-hall in Michel Delving. Aesseledh has directed you to speak with Annie Hayhurst to look at what recipes she sells.\n",
[7633]="70043023\n1\tAragorn can be found at his camp to the north-west of Pelargir. You have been summoned by Aragorn to aid his forces as he presses eastward into Gondor.\t\n2\tTalk to Aragorn at his camp outside Pelargir\tAragorn can be found at his camp to the north-west of Pelargir. You have been summoned by Aragorn to aid his forces as he presses eastward into Gondor.\n3\tMeet Angbor at the eastern gates of Pelargir\tAngbor can be found near the eastern gates of Pelargir. Aragorn has asked you to meet Lord Angbor in Pelargir before venturing into the lands of Upper Lebennin and Lossarnach.\n",
[7634]="70058241\n1\tThe fortress of Skarháld can be found in Ered Mithrin. You should travel to Skarháld.\t\n2\tTalk to Agátur the Boastful in Skarháld\tThe fortress of Skarháld can be found in Ered Mithrin. You should talk to Agátur the Boastful in Skarháld.\n3\tTalk to Rúzat at the Rushgate\tThe Rushgate can be found on the border between Ered Mithrin and Elderslade. You should talk to Rúzat at the Rushgate.\n",
[7635]="70044EDB\n1\tLamlor can be found at the First Circle of Minas Tirith. You have been summoned by Lamlor to aid Gondor on the eve of battle.\t\n2\tSpeak with Lamlor at the First Circle of Minas Tirith\tLamlor can be found at the First Circle of Minas Tirith. You have been summoned by Lamlor to aid Gondor on the eve of battle.\n3\tSpeak with Bregdal at Crithost in Talath Anor\tBregdal can be found in the village of Crithost in Talath Anor. You should seek out and speak with Bregdal.\n4\tInvestigate the drumming sounds\tThe drumming sounds are coming from an area in the forest north-west of the Grey Wood. You should investigate the drumming sounds.\n5\tSpeak with the chieftain of the Drúedain\tGhân-buri-Ghân is in the village of Drû Bhûta in Taur Drúadan. You should speak with Ghân-buri-Ghân, the chieftain of the Drúedain.\n",
[7636]="70053E30\n1\tTravel to Echad Uial\tEchad Uial can be found in Rath Dúath. You should travel to Echad Uial.\n2\tTalk to Damrod\030Talk to Thurindol\tDamrod and Thurindol can be found at Echad Uial. You should talk to Damrod and Thurindol.\n3\tComplete quests in Rath Dúath to establish a hold in the area (total: 15)\tComplete quests in Rath Dúath to establish a hold in the area.\n4\tTalk to Damrod\tDamrod can be found at Echad Uial. You should talk to Damrod.\n",
[7637]="70015700\n1\tTalk to Aldúlf, the Jeweller's Guild-leader\tAldúlf, the Jeweller's Guild-leader is in the Guild-hall in Esteldín. The Master of Crafting Guilds has instructed you to speak with Aldúlf to learn more about the Jeweller's Guild.\n2\tTalk to the vendor who sells guild symbol recipes\tThe vendor Mirchiril is in the Jeweller's Guild-hall in Esteldín. Aldúlf, the Jeweller's Guild-leader, has asked you to speak with Mirchiril to get further acquainted with the advantages of belonging to a Craft Guild.\n3\tTalk to the vendor who sells improved recipes\tThe vendor Porto Hornblower is in the Jeweller's Guild-hall in Esteldín. Aldúlf, the Jeweller's Guild-leader, has asked you to speak with Porto to get further acquainted with the advantages of belonging to a Craft Guild.\n",
[7638]="700156FE\n1\tTalk to Hávar, the Metalsmith's Guild-leader\tHávar, the Metalsmith's Guild-leader, is in the Guild-hall in Thorin's Hall. The Master of Crafting Guilds has instructed you to speak with Hávar to learn more about the Metalsmith's Guild.\n2\tTalk to the vendor who sells crest recipes\tReifnir is in the Metalsmith's Guild-hall in Thorin's Hall. Hávar has directed you to speak with Reifnir to look at what recipes he sells.\n3\tTalk to the vendor who sells improved recipes\tLar is in the Metalsmith's Guild-hall in Thorin's Hall. Hávar has directed you to speak with Lar to look at what recipes he sells.\n",
[7639]="7004CB64\n1\tGaladriel can be found either at the Court of Celeborn or in Caras Galadhon. You should speak with Galadriel.\t\n2\tGaladriel can be found either at the Court of Celeborn or in Caras Galadhon. You should speak with Galadriel.\t\n3\tSpeak with King Thranduil in the halls of Felegoth, in Eryn Lasgalen\tKing Thranduil can be found in Felegoth, in Eryn Lasgalen. A swift horse in Southern Mirkwood will bring you to Tham Taerdol in Eryn Lasgalen, not far from the Elvenking's halls. Find such a swift horse in the ruins of Ost Galadh, in Emyn Lûm.\n",
[7640]="70044101\n1\tMablung can be found at his hideout within the culverts of Osgiliath. You have been summoned by Mablung to aid Gondor as the Enemy presses closer to the city of Minas Tirith.\t\n2\tTalk to Mablung at the Ranger hideout in Osgiliath\tMablung can be found at his hideout within the culverts of Osgiliath. You have been summoned by Mablung to aid Gondor as the Enemy presses closer to the city of Minas Tirith.\n3\tTalk to Damrod at the Ranger hideout in Osgiliath\tDamrod can be found at the Ithilien Ranger hideout within the culverts of Osgiliath. You have been asked by Mablung to aid Damrod in leading the Rangers out of Osgiliath.\n4\tTravel to Minas Tirith and speak with Curugond\tMaster Builder Curugond can be found in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, near the Lower Stables. You have asked by Damrod to speak to Curugond after you make the journey to Minas Tirith.\n",
[7641]="70015701\n1\tTalk to Ethel Applegarth, the Scholar's Guild-leader\tEthel Applegarth, the Scholar's Guild-leader, is in the Guild-hall in Rivendell. The Master of Crafting Guilds has instructed you to speak with Ethel Applegarth to learn more about the Scholar's Guild.\n2\tTalk to the scroll recipe vendor\tMelongene Took is in the Scholar's Guild-hall in Rivendell. Ethel Applegarth has directed you to speak with Melongene to look at what recipes she sells.\n3\tTalk to the vendor who sells improved recipes\tSpiall is in the Scholar's Guild-hall in Rivendell. Ethel Applegarth has directed you to speak with Spiall to look at what recipes he sells.\n",
[7642]="70072714\n1\tSpeak with the Steward of Mûr Ghala, Calúrmin, at Sul Madásh\030Speak with the Steward of Mûr Ghala, Lejâl, at Zajâna\tYou were directed to speak with a Steward of Mûr Ghala to expand the breadth and impact of your assistance in the land. You should seek the counsel of Lejâl in Zajâna or Calúrmin in Sul Madásh.\n",
[7643]="700156FF\n1\tTalk to Hambrennil, the Tailor's Guild-leader\tHambrennil, the Tailor's Guild-leader is in the Guild-hall in Esteldín. The Master of Crafting Guilds has instructed you to speak with Hambrennil to learn more about the Tailor's Guild.\n2\tTalk to the pattern recipe vendor\tJarmárr is in the Tailor's Guild-hall in Esteldín. Hambrennil has directed you to speak with Jarmárr to look at what recipes he sells.\n3\tTalk to the vendor who sells improved recipes\tToby Eatwell is in the Tailor's Guild-hall in Esteldín. Hambrennil has directed you to speak with Toby Eatwell to look at what recipes he sells.\n",
[7644]="7004E327\n1\tTBD\t\n2\tTBD\t\n",
[7645]="70047B9D\n1\tDamrod can be found at the Camp of the Host in Northern Ithilien. You have been summoned by Damrod to aid the Rangers of Ithilien as they make preparations for the march to the Black Gate.\t\n2\tTalk to Damrod at the Camp of the Host\tDamrod can be found at the Camp of the Host in Northern Ithilien. You have been summoned by Damrod to aid the Rangers of Ithilien as they make preparations for the march to the Black Gate.\n3\tTalk to Mablung at the Camp of the Host\tMablung can be found at the Camp of the Host in Northern Ithilien. Mablung commands the Rangers of Ithilien stationed at the Camp of the Host and will be able to give you orders.\n",
[7646]="7002692D\n1\tTalk to Halthor Goldeneye\tSpeak with Halthor Goldeneye in the Treasure-hunter's Camp in Ered Luin.\n2\tTalk to Tór Wayseeker\tSpeak with Tór Wayseeker in the Treasure-hunters' Camp to learn about digging up buried treasure.\n3\tExcavate a dig-site in the Training Grounds\030Enter the Training Grounds\tEnter the Novice Training Grounds and use your pick.\n4\tReturn the Novice Pick to Tór Wayseeker\tReturn to Tór Wayseeker in the Treasure-hunters' Camp.\n5\tTalk to Orn Gemfinder\tTalk to Orn Gemfinder in the Treasure-hunters' Camp.\n6\tSelect a Dig-site and use the dowsing gem\030Enter the Training Grounds\tEnter the Training Grounds and use the dowsing gem in your inventory.\n7\tTalk to Orn Gemfinder\tReturn to Orn Gemfinder in the Treasure-hunters' Camp.\n8\tTalk to Segar\tSpeak with Segar in the Treasure-hunters' Camp.\n9\tUse the cave-claw in your inventory\030Enter the Training Grounds\tEnter the Training Grounds and use the cave-claw in your inventory.\n10\tTalk to Segar\tReturn to Segar in the Treasure-hunters' Camp.\n11\tTalk to Halthor Goldeneye\tTalk to Halthor Goldeneye in the Treasure-hunters' Camp.\n12\tTalk to Arngills\tTalk to Arngills in the Treasure Field.\n",
[7647]="70052962\n1\tThe Black Book of Mordor will bring you to the Vales of Anduin in Chapter 10\tThe Dwarves of the North still need your help before you venture to the Vales of Anduin. If you are interested in following the storyline of the Black Book of Mordor, Chapter 10 will bring you naturally to the Vales of Anduin. Chapter 9 is available by speaking with Durin on the upper level of Skarháld.\n2\tTalk to Legolas at the Forest Gate in Eryn Lasgalen\030Complete 'The Black Book of Mordor, Chapter 10.1: A New Journey'\tThe Black Book of Mordor will bring you to the Vales of Anduin in Chapter 10. Legolas can be found at the Forest Gate between Eryn Lasgalen and the Vales of Anduin.\n3\tTalk to Grimbeorn\tGrimbeorn can be found at the Beorninghús in the Beorning-lands. You should talk to Grimbeorn.\n",
[7648]="70052968\n1\tTalk to Legolas at the Forest Gate in Eryn Lasgalen\tLegolas can be found at the Forest Gate between Eryn Lasgalen and the Vales of Anduin. You should talk to Legolas about King Thranduil's request to open the trade route through the Beorning-lands in the Vales of Anduin.\n2\tTalk to Legolas at the Forest Gate in Eryn Lasgalen\tLegolas can be found at the Forest Gate between Eryn Lasgalen and the Vales of Anduin. You should talk to Legolas about King Thranduil's request to open the trade route through the Beorning-lands in the Vales of Anduin.\n3\tTalk to Grimbeorn\tGrimbeorn can be found at the Beorninghús in the Beorninglands of the Vales of Anduin. You should talk to Grimbeorn.\n",
})
